  "plugin": "claimcheck",
  "version": "v0.1.0",
  "homepage": "https://github.com/asaleem9/claimcheck",
  "description": "claimcheck replays kube-scheduler's own Dynamic Resource Allocation\nallocator against your cluster and explains, device by device, why a\nResourceClaim can't be allocated: failing CEL selectors with the actual\nattribute values, devices held by other claims, device taints, constraint\nand shared-counter conflicts, and requests that compete for the same\ndevices. It can also suggest the single change that would let a pod fit,\nshow pool fragmentation, and run offline from a snapshot file. Read-only.\n",
